<%#
  A run that stopped somewhere it cannot rest.

  Either it is sitting on a sub_flow node, which has no UI of its own, or it is
  waiting on a child scenario that has already finished. Both used to be healed
  inside GET step, which made a read move the run. Resuming needs a POST, so it
  gets a control: a stuck run is visible rather than silently repaired, and the
  fact that it happened at all is a bug worth seeing.

  Normal runs never reach this — ScenarioSettler leaves every POST on a step
  someone can answer.

  locals: next_url
%>
<div class="card">
  <div class="card__body">
    <h2 class="mb-2">This run is paused</h2>
    <p class="text-sm mb-4" style="color: var(--color-ink-muted);">
      It stopped between steps. Continue to pick it up where it left off.
    </p>
    <%= button_to "Resume", next_url, class: "btn btn--primary" %>
  </div>
</div>
